# VitruvianSoftware Monorepo CODEOWNERS
#
# This file defines default code owners for vitruvian-core.
# Location: .github/CODEOWNERS (GitHub's preferred path).
#
# OWNERSHIP MODEL (per-app teams)
# ===============================
# Ownership routes to per-app / platform teams in the VitruvianSoftware org
# (issue #460). Each team currently has a single member (@ipv1337); adding a
# maintainer to an area is now a team-membership change, not a CODEOWNERS edit.
# Teams (created + granted repo access, codified in
# infrastructure/pulumi/platform/repo_config):
#    @VitruvianSoftware/platform-team              platform / build / infra
#    @VitruvianSoftware/devx-team                  devx
#    @VitruvianSoftware/homelab-team               homelab
#    @VitruvianSoftware/mcp-slack-team             mcp-slack
#    @VitruvianSoftware/nexus-agent-team           nexus-agent
#    @VitruvianSoftware/tabula-team                tabula
#    @VitruvianSoftware/oauth-user-inspector-team  oauth-user-inspector
#
# IMPORTANT: "Require review from Code Owners" is deliberately STILL OFF.
# ======================================================================
# Every team has a single member today, so a solo code owner cannot approve
# their own PR — requiring code-owner review would block ALL merges, including
# hotfixes. CODEOWNERS therefore ROUTES review (suggested reviewers) but does
# not GATE it. Enable required code-owner review per-area only once that team
# has a second member (see the conformance guard proposed in #460 / #82).
#
# References:
# - Issue #460: Create per-app CODEOWNERS teams in repo-config
# - Issue #82:  CODEOWNERS + inter-app Bazel visibility boundaries
# - Issue #76:  External-contribution model (Copybara one-way + PR-import)
#
# See https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# NOTE on pattern ordering: CODEOWNERS uses "last matching pattern wins".
# Repo-root build/module config patterns are anchored with a leading "/" so they
# match ONLY the repo root and do not re-own each app's nested BUILD file.

# Default: catch-all for the whole repository
* @VitruvianSoftware/platform-team

# Repo-root build and module configuration files
# (leading "/" anchors these to the root only; nested per-app BUILD files
#  remain owned by their app directory rule above)
# ================================================
/.bazelrc @VitruvianSoftware/platform-team
/.bazelversion @VitruvianSoftware/platform-team
/MODULE.bazel @VitruvianSoftware/platform-team
/MODULE.bazel.lock @VitruvianSoftware/platform-team
/BUILD @VitruvianSoftware/platform-team

# Platform, build, and infrastructure paths
# ==========================================
/.github/ @VitruvianSoftware/platform-team
/githooks/ @VitruvianSoftware/platform-team
/tools/ @VitruvianSoftware/platform-team
/infrastructure/ @VitruvianSoftware/platform-team
/gitops/ @VitruvianSoftware/platform-team
/pulumi/ @VitruvianSoftware/platform-team
/packages/ @VitruvianSoftware/platform-team

# Application directories (per-app teams)
# =======================================
/devx/ @VitruvianSoftware/devx-team
/homelab/ @VitruvianSoftware/homelab-team
/mcp-slack/ @VitruvianSoftware/mcp-slack-team
/nexus-agent/ @VitruvianSoftware/nexus-agent-team
/oauth-user-inspector/ @VitruvianSoftware/oauth-user-inspector-team
/tabula/ @VitruvianSoftware/tabula-team
